course: dictionary
lesson: 589
title: Autopilot: one word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: An autopilot is a computer system that steers a plane, ship or car by itself, so a person does not have to do it by hand. «An autopilot is a computer that holds height, speed and direction and follows a planned route, while the pilots watch and take over.» The pilots are still there, watching. The computer does the steady work.
explain: Read the clues in the sentence: holds height, speed and direction, follows a planned route. Those words tell you what the machine keeps steady. If you swap in "a computer that steers by itself", the sentence still makes sense, so your meaning works.
explain: The word has a second meaning in everyday talk. When someone is "on autopilot", they do something without thinking, out of habit, like walking to school and not noticing the way. The context tells you which meaning is meant: is it a plane, or a person's mind?
fact: An autopilot is a computer system that steers and controls an aircraft, ship or car automatically.
fact: Pilots still watch the autopilot and take over for some jobs, such as take-off and landing, or when there is trouble.
fact: Some planes can even land themselves in thick fog.
fact: "On autopilot" means doing something without thinking about it, out of habit.
fact: "Switch on the autopilot" is a useful phrase, and autopilot is a noun.
exercise: «An autopilot is a computer that holds height, speed and direction.» What does an autopilot do? | It is a map for tourists | It flies the plane by a person's hand alone | It makes the engine louder | *It steers and controls a plane, ship or car automatically
exercise: Ben says, «He drove to school on autopilot, not noticing a single street.» What does "on autopilot" mean here? | Driving very fast | Driving with the lights on | *Doing something without thinking, out of habit | Driving a computer-controlled car
exercise: «...while the pilots watch and take over.» Find and copy the word that means keeping an eye on something. | *watch | route | fog | height
test: «Some planes can even land themselves in thick fog.» What does this tell you about autopilots? | Planes never land in fog | Pilots must always land by hand | Fog makes autopilots switch off | *Some can control landing without a person doing it by hand
test: Mia says autopilot only means a machine in planes. Why is she wrong? | Autopilot is a kind of car horn | Planes do not have autopilots | *It can also mean doing something without thinking, out of habit | It only means a pilot's seat
exam: Dad says he got home "on autopilot" after a long day. What does he mean? | He used a computer to drive the car home | He was a pilot in a hurry | He was flying a plane home | *He got home without really thinking about the way, out of habit
